    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0536" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Bullitt, William C./551: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-12-22T22:00:00-05:00">December 22, 1939—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1559. Your 3023, December 21, 8 p.m. From the President and the Secretary.
                    Daladier is asking us to assume greater responsibility than is possible.
                    Practically speaking it might well react against the very purpose he has in
                    mind. Please make this clear to him and explain why we cannot order you home at
                    this time but will do so when Kennedy<anchor n="60" xml:id="d472-f1"/> returns
                    to London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d472-f1" n="60" xml:id="d472-f1-content">
                <p>Joseph P. Kennedy, Ambassador in the United Kingdom.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
